window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-sakagami"]=[{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p193-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 6 sec  6 1  class c s teacher at the table the student council room  he sits beside his three students   a bespectacled male teacher in his 30s  homeroom teacher of class c  present as the accused class s teacher   then can it really be considered self defense when fighting against opponents of such unequal strength   but only the class c students were hurt  he smiles the moment sudo calls the others wimps  the narrator catches the expression and treats the question as a trap laid for exactly that answer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p193-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: Class C&#x27;s teacher at the table<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.193–196<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The student council room; he sits beside his three students, &quot;a bespectacled male teacher in his 30s.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Then can it really be considered self-defense when fighting against opponents of such unequal strength?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;But only the Class C students were hurt.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Homeroom teacher of Class C, present as the accused class&#x27;s teacher.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He smiles the moment Sudō calls the others wimps; the narrator catches the expression and treats the question as a trap laid for exactly that answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p199-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the attack on the witness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p199-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 6 sec  6 1  the attack on the witness  i thought i d heard something or other about a witness  but you re a class d student   apparently she didn t witness anything  more of this would just be a waste of our time   i want to speed this along  if we waste time  my students will suffer  these students are the joyful heart of their class  so i ve no doubt that their many friends are worried about them  also  they re striving to improve their basketball skills  and we re depriving them of valuable practice time  as a teacher  i can t overlook this   excuse me  but may i say something   normally  teachers are asked to speak as little as possible  but this situation is just too pitiful  student council president  do you mind   in regards to what you ve said  sakura kun  i do not necessarily doubt you  however  i have one thing to ask  you ve stepped forward to testify as a witness  but you were rather late in doing so  may i ask why  i would think if you really did see something  you would have come forward much earlier   why didn t you want to get involved   i see  i understand that  however  i d like to say something else  you re not good at talking with others  and yet when the week was nearly out you stepped forward as a witness  doesn t that seem rather odd  to my mind  it seems class d secretly put a story together and are having you act as a false witness to give phony testimony   no matter how poor your communication skills might be  i can see you haven t testified with much confidence  is that because you re tormented with guilt  because you know what you re saying is actually a lie   i m not blaming you  you were probably forced to lie for your class s sake  to save sudou kun  weren t you  if you come forward and confess honestly to us now  you won t be punished   i don t think so  there are excellent students in class d  students such as yourself  horikita san  by setting up a person like sakura san as your witness  it would establish a sense of realism that you yourself could not  the cross examination is built to make the witness doubt herself rather than to test her account  the narrator s read is that  sakagami sensei probably didn t actually believe this   please  let s not force this situation to continue  if there really was evidence  you would have presented it at an earlier stage","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p199-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the attack on the witness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.199–203<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I thought I’d heard something or other about a witness, but you’re a Class D student?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Apparently she didn’t witness anything. More of this would just be a waste of our time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I want to speed this along. If we waste time, my students will suffer. These students are the joyful heart of their class, so I’ve no doubt that their many friends are worried about them. Also, they’re striving to improve their…<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I want to speed this along. If we waste time, my students will suffer. These students are the joyful heart of their class, so I’ve no doubt that their many friends are worried about them. Also, they’re striving to improve their basketball skills, and we’re depriving them of valuable practice time. As a teacher, I can’t overlook this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Excuse me, but may I say something?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Normally, teachers are asked to speak as little as possible, but this situation is just too pitiful. Student council president, do you mind?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In regards to what you’ve said, Sakura-kun, I do not necessarily doubt you. However, I have one thing to ask. You’ve stepped forward to testify as a witness, but you were rather late in doing so. May I ask why? I would think if you really did see something, you would have come forward much earlier.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Why didn’t you want to get involved?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. I understand that. However, I’d like to say something else. You’re not good at talking with others, and yet when the week was nearly out you stepped forward as a witness. Doesn’t that seem rather odd? To my mind, it seems Class D secretly put a story together and are having you act as a false witness to give phony testimony.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No matter how poor your communication skills might be, I can see you haven’t testified with much confidence. Is that because you’re tormented with guilt, because you know what you’re saying is actually a lie?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m not blaming you. You were probably forced to lie for your class’s sake, to save Sudou-kun. Weren’t you? If you come forward and confess honestly to us now, you won’t be punished.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t think so. There are excellent students in Class D, students such as yourself, Horikita-san. By setting up a person like Sakura-san as your witness, it would establish a sense of realism that you yourself could not.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The cross-examination is built to make the witness doubt herself rather than to test her account; the narrator&#x27;s read is that &quot;Sakagami-sensei probably didn&#x27;t actually believe this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please, let’s not force this situation to continue. If there really was evidence, you would have presented it at an earlier stage—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p193-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: Class C&#x27;s teacher at the table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p204-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the photographs, and the compromise<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p204-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 6 sec  6 1  the photographs  and the compromise  what did you use to take these photos   you can alter the date rather easily with a digital camera  though  if you manipulated these photos on a computer  you could effectively set them at the time and date of the incident  this are inadequate evidence  the run together  this are inadequate evidence  is kept as printed  the page calls him  sakagamisensei s  once  in the run together form   sakagamisensei s expression stiffened for the first time   th this   i see  well  you do seem to be telling the truth about witnessing the incident  that much i simply must accept  however  i can t ascertain how the situation started from this picture  this doesn t prove that you saw the entire incident   so  what do you think  chabashira sensei  why not look for a compromise here   i m convinced that sudou kun lied in his testimony   no matter how long we go back and forth  we ll never reach an agreement  we won t change our testimony  and your side won t give up or admit that you conspired with the witness  in other words  you won t stop  it ll be an endless cycle of saying that the other side is lying  in addition  the picture is too inconclusive to be considered definitive proof  therefore  i suggest we compromise  i do think that the students from class c are responsible for some of the blame here  there were three students up against sudou  and one of them has a history of fighting  which is a problem  so how about two weeks of suspension for sudou kun  and one week of suspension for my students  what do you think of that  the weight of the punishment is different  of course  but i think that matches the difference in sustained injuries   chabashira sensei  what do you think  the proposal is a settlement that still assigns sudo the larger share  the narrator calls it  asking for less than half  of a month and therefore  a considerable concession  for class c","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p204-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the photographs, and the compromise<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.204–205<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What did you use to take these photos?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You can alter the date rather easily with a digital camera, though. If you manipulated these photos on a computer, you could effectively set them at the time and date of the incident. This are inadequate evidence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Th-this?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The run-together &quot;This are inadequate evidence&quot; is kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page calls him &quot;Sakagamisensei’s&quot; once, in the run-together form: &quot;Sakagamisensei’s expression stiffened for the first time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203–204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. Well, you do seem to be telling the truth about witnessing the incident. That much I simply must accept. However, I can’t ascertain how the situation started from this picture. This doesn’t prove that you saw the entire incident.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So, what do you think, Chabashira-sensei? Why not look for a compromise here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m convinced that Sudou-kun lied in his testimony.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No matter how long we go back and forth, we’ll never reach an agreement. We won’t change our testimony, and your side won’t give up or admit that you conspired with the witness. In other words, you won’t stop. It’ll be an endless cycle of saying that the other side is lying. In addition, the picture is too inconclusive to be considered definitive proof. Therefore, I suggest we compromise. I do think that the students from Class C are responsible for some of the blame here. There were three students up against Sudou, and one of them has a history of fighting, which is a problem. So how about two weeks of suspension for Sudou-kun, and one week of suspension for my students? What do you think of that? The weight of the punishment is different, of course, but I think that matches the difference in sustained injuries.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Chabashira-sensei. What do you think?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The proposal is a settlement that still assigns Sudō the larger share; the narrator calls it &quot;asking for less than half&quot; of a month and therefore &quot;a considerable concession&quot; for Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p199-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the attack on the witness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p208-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the two verdicts<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p208-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi chabashira-sae sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 6 sec  6 1  the two verdicts  ha ha  what can i even say  we did this intentionally  what a bizarre claim  apparently  the student council president s younger sister can t help but spew nonsense   i want you to reflect on the fact that many students will be involved in this due to your lies  also  if you think that we ll go easy on you if you start crying  then i am afraid you are being foolish  you should be ashamed of yourself  the parting speech is delivered to sakura on the way out  after the hearing has ended and no one can answer it  the chapter gives no reply  he treats her testimony as a class fabrication and tells her  at the door  that the harm is hers  he addresses the compromise to her first  and she accepts it before class d answers","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p208-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the two verdicts<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.208–209<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ha ha… What can I even say? We did this intentionally? What a bizarre claim. Apparently, the student council president’s younger sister can’t help but spew nonsense.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I want you to reflect on the fact that many students will be involved in this due to your lies. Also, if you think that we’ll go easy on you if you start crying, then I am afraid you are being foolish. You should be ashamed of…<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I want you to reflect on the fact that many students will be involved in this due to your lies. Also, if you think that we’ll go easy on you if you start crying, then I am afraid you are being foolish. You should be ashamed of yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The parting speech is delivered to Sakura on the way out, after the hearing has ended and no one can answer it; the chapter gives no reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> He treats her testimony as a class fabrication and tells her, at the door, that the harm is hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.199–209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> He addresses the compromise to her first, and she accepts it before Class D answers.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p204-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the photographs, and the compromise<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p243-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: he loses his students in the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p243-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"chabashira-sae sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 7 sec  7 5  he loses his students in the room  oh  my  i see that the boy from yesterday isn t here   well  whatever  it s up to you guys to decide   you made it just in the nick of time    a slight sigh of relief when his three students arrive  well then  we would like to resume deliberations on this case  from where we left off yesterday  please take your seat   what is it   what are you  what in the world do you mean    standing up at the request not to hold the trial  what s so funny  chabashira sensei  he  did not seem to like her attitude  glaring at chabashira sensei in irritation   what did you do  threaten my students with violence so they d withdraw their appeal   there s no way that my students would withdraw their complaint unless you had  tell us the truth  if you do that  then we can do something about it  unable to comprehend what his students are saying  he hangs his head low and sits back down  he leaves slowly with his students  and when the door closes  he started hounding his students for answers  he takes her amusement at the withdrawal as an affront and answers it with a glare","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p243-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: he loses his students in the room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.243–246<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Oh, my. I see that the boy from yesterday isn’t here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, whatever. It’s up to you guys to decide.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You made it just in the nick of time,&quot; — a slight sigh of relief when his three students arrive<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, we would like to resume deliberations on this case, from where we left off yesterday. Please take your seat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What is it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What are you…? What in the world do you mean?&quot; — standing up at the request not to hold the trial<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What’s so funny, Chabashira-sensei?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He &quot;did not seem to like her attitude, glaring at Chabashira-sensei in irritation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What did you do? Threaten my students with violence so they’d withdraw their appeal?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s no way that my students would withdraw their complaint unless you had. Tell us the truth. If you do that, then we can do something about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Unable to comprehend what his students are saying, he hangs his head low and sits back down.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He leaves slowly with his students, and when the door closes &quot;he started hounding his students for answers.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> He takes her amusement at the withdrawal as an affront and answers it with a glare.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v2-p208-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the two verdicts<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v4-p122-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 3  named in the teachers  corner hoshinomiya names him while she drinks with chabashira and mashima  sakagami sensei is called part of the problem in how the classes are evaluated","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v4-p122-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: named in the teachers’ corner<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.122<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hoshinomiya names him while she drinks with Chabashira and Mashima.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakagami-sensei is called part of the problem in how the classes are evaluated.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v6-p179-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru chabashira-sae sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 7  first to take an envelope appears at the staff room first and takes ryuuen s manila envelope before chabashira takes horikita s  takes his submission  takes sakagami s place moments later  named only in the handover sequence  no dialogue","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v6-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: first to take an envelope<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.179<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears at the staff room first and takes Ryuuen’s manila envelope before Chabashira takes Horikita’s.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Takes his submission.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Takes Sakagami’s place moments later.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named only in the handover sequence; no dialogue.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v7-p120-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 5 sec  5 1  the closing homeroom and the camera debt class c s teacher closes the second semester  later pages remember the earlier camera painting report   i d like to remind everyone to please be on your best behavior  even during winter vacation  and to make good use of your time  that s all  ryuuen listens to what he calls gracious  meaningless words  then turns to his own plan  named only as the teacher ryuuen reported a earlier spray painted camera to  the punishment was paying for cleaning","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v7-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the closing homeroom and the camera debt<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.120, 126<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class C’s teacher closes the second semester; later pages remember the earlier camera-painting report.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’d like to remind everyone to please be on your best behavior, even during winter vacation, and to make good use of your time. That’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen listens to what he calls gracious, meaningless words, then turns to his own plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named only as the teacher Ryuuen reported a earlier spray-painted camera to; the punishment was paying for cleaning.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v7-p201-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the first and last chance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v7-p201-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi yamada-albert ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 7  the first and last chance takes ryuuen s next day appointment in the faculty room  then walks him through the camera and fight report in the counselor s office   i understand   please accompany me to the counselor s office   but first  there s something we must address   would you step outside  please   they ve been waiting since early this morning  wondering whether you d come by  even when i told them to contact you directly  they wouldn t listen  quite troublesome  before we have our meeting  i need you to do something about these two   about the surveillance camera being destroyed did these two have anything to do with it   i have a general idea of what happened  based on what you said over the phone  but walk me through this once more  ryuuen  first of all  you admit to defacing the security camera by spray painting the lens   okay  one more thing  is it true that a fight broke out between you  ishizaki  albert  and ibuki   well then  this ll be quick   ryuuen   it seems there s a misunderstanding here  so allow me to offer some corrections   we ve confirmed that there are inconsistencies in your statement   based on my understanding  there s some kind of problem between you and class d   a complaint  no  from what i ve heard  a single class d student was also involved in destroying the security camera   class d already paid the private points necessary to cover the repair  what i wanted to confirm with you was whether you wished to split the blame   there s no problem here  though  you still want to drop out  despite that   i see  if that s your final decision  i can t stop you   please write your name  student id number  and reason for withdrawal on this form   once we finish processing your withdrawal  please deliver these to ishizaki and yamada   you re certainly right  but this was their wish  they said that  should you choose to drop out of school  they would quit too  they wouldn t listen to reason   personally  i would find it rather regrettable for anyone in my class to drop out   as things stand  the matter can be resolved with a simple punishment for damaging school property  this is your first and last chance  takes the confession seriously  then turns the paperwork into the trap that keeps his student enrolled  the homeroom teacher who offers the last chance  one of the two waiters and form recipients  the other  the class d student who already paid the repair   cited without a name by sakagami  the former president whose prior knowledge forces the report timing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v7-p201-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the first and last chance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.201–204<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Takes Ryuuen’s next-day appointment in the faculty room, then walks him through the camera and fight report in the counselor’s office.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I understand,”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Please accompany me to the counselor’s office.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“But first, there’s something we must address.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you step outside, please?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “They’ve been waiting since early this morning, wondering whether you’d come by. Even when I told them to contact you directly, they wouldn’t listen. Quite troublesome. Before we have our meeting, I need you to do something about these two,”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “About the surveillance camera being destroyed—did these two have anything to do with it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have a general idea of what happened, based on what you said over the phone, but walk me through this once more, Ryuuen. First of all, you admit to defacing the security camera by spray-painting the lens?”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, one more thing. Is it true that a fight broke out between you, Ishizaki, Albert, and Ibuki?”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, this’ll be quick.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ryuuen?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems there’s a misunderstanding here, so allow me to offer some corrections,”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ve confirmed that there are inconsistencies in your statement.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Based on my understanding, there’s some kind of problem between you and Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A complaint? No, from what I’ve heard, a single Class D student was also involved in destroying the security camera.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class D already paid the private points necessary to cover the repair. What I wanted to confirm with you was whether you wished to split the blame.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no problem here, though. You still want to drop out, despite that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. If that’s your final decision, I can’t stop you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please write your name, student ID number, and reason for withdrawal on this form.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Once we finish processing your withdrawal, please deliver these to Ishizaki and Yamada.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re certainly right. But this was their wish. They said that, should you choose to drop out of school, they would quit too. They wouldn’t listen to reason.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Personally, I would find it rather regrettable for anyone in my class to drop out,”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As things stand, the matter can be resolved with a simple punishment for damaging school property. This is your first and last chance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes the confession seriously, then turns the paperwork into the trap that keeps his student enrolled.<span class=\"pg\">p.201–204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The homeroom teacher who offers the last chance.<span class=\"pg\">p.201–204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> One of the two waiters and form recipients.<span class=\"pg\">p.201–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> The other.<span class=\"pg\">p.201–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The Class D student who already paid the repair — cited without a name by Sakagami.<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The former president whose prior knowledge forces the report timing.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v7-p120-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the closing homeroom and the camera debt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v11-p404-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakayanagi-arisu hoshinomiya-chie tsukishiro sakagami","q":"sakagami epilogue  proctoring the final event directs the start of the chess event as proctor  announces class a s victory in the chess event and the special exam  reprimands hoshinomiya for joking with ayanokoji and tells the students they may leave  questions the outside workers brought in by tsukishiro but complies when told to leave  proctors his match and announces the result  proctors her match against ayanokoji  works alongside her during and after the exam  defers to his authority and leaves the multipurpose room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v11-p404-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Proctoring the final event<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.404–438<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Directs the start of the chess event as proctor. Announces Class A’s victory in the chess event and the special exam. Reprimands Hoshinomiya for joking with Ayanokōji and tells the students they may leave. Questions the outside workers brought in by Tsukishiro but complies when told to leave.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Proctors his match and announces the result.<span class=\"pg\">p.404–431<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Proctors her match against Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.404–429<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Works alongside her during and after the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.404–437<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Defers to his authority and leaves the multipurpose room.<span class=\"pg\">p.437–438<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v11-p431-1\">→ After: Epilogue: After the exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v11-p431-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie sakagami","q":"sakagami epilogue  after the exam says the students are done for the day   no  you re done for today  you re free to go straight home if you want  cleans up with her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v11-p431-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: After the exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.431<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Says the students are done for the day.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, you’re done for today. You’re free to go straight home if you want.”<span class=\"pg\">p.431<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Cleans up with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.431<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y1v11-p404-1\">← Before: Epilogue: Proctoring the final event<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y1v11_5-p47-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"","w":"tsukishiro sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 1  chess exam meeting participates in the meeting with ayanokoji  sakayanagi  tsukishiro  and other teachers concerning the chess exam  hears sakayanagi claim that ayanokoji was the original winner of the chess game and that the process was manipulated  takes part in the teachers  response as the issue of acting director tsukishiro s interference is pressed  confronts the acting director over exam interference  hears her accusation regarding the chess exam  present in the meeting involving his exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y1v11_5-p47-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Chess exam meeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.47–87<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Participates in the meeting with Ayanokōji, Sakayanagi, Tsukishiro, and other teachers concerning the chess exam. Hears Sakayanagi claim that Ayanokōji was the original winner of the chess game and that the process was manipulated. Takes part in the teachers’ response as the issue of Acting Director Tsukishiro’s interference is pressed.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Confronts the acting director over exam interference.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Hears her accusation regarding the chess exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Present in the meeting involving his exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v1-p344-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami epilogue  mention mentioned in passing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v1-p344-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.344<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mentioned in passing.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v3-p150-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakagami","q":"sakagami sakagami at the water race task a teacher  class 2 b homeroom  caught early while setting up a task site near the h4 center  ayanokoji calls out to sign up for the first second spots  the water race task  his delivery of 2l 1 5l and the points   hello   oh  ayanokoji   is it alright if we re the first ones to sign up  sakagami sensei   yes   this is a task where you earn water according to the order in which you arrive  a race  essentially  ayanokoji  having come in first  will receive 2 liters of water and three points  as you came in second  nanase  you ll receive 1 5 liters of water and two points   well then  you can register for the task now   luck is also an extension of your abilities  you two  be proud  task registration paperwork handled before the clock struck 3 30  his task  order of arrival water race   ak first  2l 3 points  nanase second  1 5l 2 points","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v3-p150-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakagami at the water-race Task<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.150–151<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A teacher (Class 2-B homeroom) caught early while setting up a Task site near the H4 center; Ayanokōji calls out to sign up for the first/second spots; the water-race Task; his delivery of 2L/1.5L and the points.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Hello.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh… Ayanokōji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Is it alright if we’re the first ones to sign up, Sakagami-sensei?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a Task where you earn water according to the order in which you arrive, a race, essentially. Ayanokōji, having come in first, will receive 2 liters of water and three points. As you came in second, Nanase, you’ll receive 1.5 liters of water and two points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, you can register for the Task now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Luck is also an extension of your abilities, you two. Be proud.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Task registration paperwork handled before the clock struck 3:30; his Task: order-of-arrival water race — AK first (2L/3 points), Nanase second (1.5L/2 points).<span class=\"pg\">p.150–151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y2v3-p193-1\">→ After: Sakagami at the scene (Ch.5)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v3-p193-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"shinohara-satsuki ike-kanji chabashira-sae sakagami","q":"sakagami sakagami at the scene  ch 5  one hour after the alert  arrives with chabashira   three medical personnel  takes charge  retells shinohara s account and razes it  the  convenient tale  verdict   let s get down to business and hear what happened here  shall we   crying isn t going to get us anywhere  i hope you know that   well  i suppose that s fine  go ahead and speak   pushed off   how awfully unsettling   if that s the truth  then yes  of course they won t   then  i assume she must have evidence of some sort to back that up  yes   so how about it  shinohara san  you can t just keep crying  so how about you give us an answer   dark  so dark that you couldn t see the culprit s face   so  it was dark to the extent that you couldn t see their face  and yet you were able to see them get pushed without any problems  it pains me to say this  but that s an awfully convenient tale you ve spun  now isn t it   you re her classmate  it s only natural that you would say that   if she s telling the truth  then this is quite a serious matter  however  this testimony alone is not enough   no matter how things play out  i d say that their only real option is retirement  as their homeroom teacher  i certainly can t say i m happy to see them withdraw from the exam either  but from the look of their legs  it would be impossible for them to continue   given the current situation  we have no choice but to conclude that shinohara san is lying in order to gloss over the injuries caused by this accident   i ll overlook that careless outburst of yours just this once  are we clear  strict  procedural  humane but locked into the school s math  he never buys the conspiracy  the expulsion of shinohara means a lighter burden for the rest of his class  the interrogation axis  the outburst he overlooks  his co examiner","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v3-p193-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakagami at the scene (Ch.5)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.193–201<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One hour after the alert; arrives with Chabashira + three medical personnel; takes charge; retells Shinohara&#x27;s account and razes it; the “convenient tale” verdict.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Let’s get down to business and hear what happened here, shall we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Crying isn’t going to get us anywhere, I hope you know that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“…Well, I suppose that’s fine. Go ahead and speak.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Pushed off? …How awfully unsettling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that’s the truth, then yes, of course they won’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, I assume she must have evidence of some sort to back that up, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So how about it, Shinohara-san? You can’t just keep crying, so how about you give us an answer?”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Dark? So dark that you couldn’t see the culprit’s face?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, it was dark to the extent that you couldn’t see their face, and yet you were able to see them get pushed without any problems…? It pains me to say this, but that’s an awfully convenient tale you’ve spun, now isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re her classmate. It’s only natural that you would say that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If she’s telling the truth, then this is quite a serious matter. However, this testimony alone is not enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No matter how things play out, I’d say that their only real option is retirement. As their homeroom teacher, I certainly can’t say I’m happy to see them withdraw from the exam either, but from the look of their legs, it would be impossible for them to continue.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Given the current situation, we have no choice but to conclude that Shinohara-san is lying in order to gloss over the injuries caused by this accident.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll overlook that careless outburst of yours just this once. Are we clear?”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Strict, procedural, humane but locked into the school&#x27;s math; he never buys the conspiracy; the expulsion of Shinohara means a lighter burden for the rest of his class.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> The interrogation axis.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The outburst he overlooks.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> His co-examiner.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y2v3-p150-1\">← Before: Sakagami at the water-race Task<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y2v3-p205-1\">→ After: Sakagami named at the gate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v3-p205-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami sakagami named at the gate  direction as sakagami sensei and the medical team    named  not present  pov ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v3-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakagami named at the gate<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.205<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “direction as Sakagami-sensei and the medical team.” — named; not present; POV Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y2v3-p193-1\">← Before: Sakagami at the scene (Ch.5)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v5-p141-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru sakagami","q":"sakagami sakagami  class d s silent referee senses ryuen approaching and distances himself from the podium  knows this is ryuen s usual stand up   yes  it is  we will now have a second round of voting  and you have 60 seconds to cast your votes   it s been explained to you in advance  but after sixty seconds  penalty time will accumulate   everyone has finished voting  now i will announce the results   since the vote was unanimous  the question has been rejected  this concludes the special exam  adjacent narration   sakagami looked up once and glanced at tokito  class d s teacher   sits at the back and lets the class run  procedural intervention only  no rescue attempt for ibuki  does not remark on the class s near miss  his quiet tormentor  ryuen s proof that no class is truly manageable by consensus alone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v5-p141-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakagami: Class D&#x27;s silent referee<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.141–166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Senses Ryūen approaching and distances himself from the podium; knows this is Ryūen&#x27;s usual stand-up.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes, it is. We will now have a second round of voting, and you have 60 seconds to cast your votes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s been explained to you in advance, but after sixty seconds, penalty time will accumulate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Everyone has finished voting. Now I will announce the results.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Since the vote was unanimous, the question has been rejected. This concludes the special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Adjacent narration: &quot;Sakagami looked up once and glanced at Tokitō.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Class D&#x27;s teacher — sits at the back and lets the class run; procedural intervention only; no rescue attempt for Ibuki; does not remark on the class&#x27;s near-miss.<span class=\"pg\">p.141–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His quiet tormentor; Ryūen&#x27;s proof that no class is truly manageable by consensus alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.141–166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v6-p212-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 4  sakagami sensei   to witness the alliance contract horikita   i intend to have chabashira sensei and sakagami sensei get involved in this as well    the karaoke deal will be formalized with sakagami sensei as a witness  the corpus prints only the surname  sakagami sensei    which sakagami is not resolved on these pages  the corpus prints only  sakagami sensei    not resolved to a given name here  both a student council sakagami and the chess club coach sakagami are plausible in world possibilities  no assignment is made  anchored references   quoted corpus verbatim where shown  see rows for pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v6-p212-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: Sakagami-sensei — to witness the alliance contract<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.212–212<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Anchored references — quoted corpus verbatim where shown; see rows for pages.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Horikita: “I intend to have Chabashira-sensei and Sakagami-sensei get involved in this as well.” — the karaoke deal will be formalized with Sakagami-sensei as a witness; the corpus prints only the surname “Sakagami-sensei” — which Sakagami is not resolved on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The corpus prints only “Sakagami-sensei” — not resolved to a given name here; both a student-council SAKAGAMI and the chess-club coach Sakagami are plausible in-world possibilities; no assignment is made.<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v7-p175-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi mashima-tomonari yagami-takuya ryuuen-kakeru sakagami","q":"sakagami the witness  the assist  2   sakagami sensei also showed up later in the student council room  with mashima sensei  sakagami sensei confirmed mashima sensei  as if remembering something  nagumo spoke first    speaking of yagami kun  i m sure mashima sensei recalls as well   it was just yesterday  we were going to have a discussion today  just me  ryuen  and komiya and kinoshita  why are the teachers here    nagumo   i called them here to save you the trouble  i heard that sakagami rushed over when the two of you were injured    nagumo  ryuen kun  excited at the start of a perfect fight  was just about to jump on yagami kun  still  mashima sensei  as a teacher  stepped in between yagami kun and ryuen kun   get lost  he kicked mashima sensei in the knee  and when he staggered over  he slammed his fist into his face  sakagami sensei witnessed it up close and took a frightened step away  ryuen kun  excited at the start of a perfect fight  was just about to jump on yagami kun  five adults steped into the student council room with blank expressions on their faces  not all of them were recognizable  but two of the five were guests of honor who had also shown up at the maid cafe  surrounded by adults  yagami kun was taken away without resistance  amasawa san walked with him   i understand    with sakagami sensei s help  mashima sensei left the student council room  the room  which had been so noisy  was suddenly enveloped in silence  he witnessed the kick in the knee and the fist to the face  he helped mashima sensei leave  he showed up  he said nothing publicly  he witnessed the removal  nagumo called him  sakagami remembered  ryuen was just about to jump on yagami kun   sakagami watched","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v7-p175-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The witness; the assist<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.175–182<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">§2 — Sakagami-sensei also showed up later in the student council room; with Mashima-sensei. Ryūen-kun, excited at the start of a perfect fight, was just about to jump on Yagami-kun. Five adults steped into the student council room with blank expressions on their faces; not all of them were recognizable, but two of the five were guests of honor who had also shown up at the maid cafe.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “I called them here to save you the trouble. I heard that Sakagami rushed over when the two of you were injured.” — Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakagami-sensei confirmed Mashima-sensei, as if remembering something; Nagumo spoke first — “Speaking of Yagami-kun, I&#x27;m sure Mashima-sensei recalls as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “It was just yesterday. We were going to have a discussion today, just me, Ryūen, and Komiya and Kinoshita. Why are the teachers here?” — Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Still, Mashima-sensei, as a teacher, stepped in between Yagami-kun and Ryūen-kun.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Get lost.” He kicked Mashima-sensei in the knee, and when he staggered over, he slammed his fist into his face.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakagami-sensei witnessed it up close and took a frightened step away.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryūen-kun, excited at the start of a perfect fight, was just about to jump on Yagami-kun.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Surrounded by adults, Yagami-kun was taken away without resistance; Amasawa-san walked with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I understand.” — with Sakagami-sensei&#x27;s help, Mashima-sensei left the student council room; the room, which had been so noisy, was suddenly enveloped in silence.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> He witnessed the kick in the knee and the fist to the face; he helped Mashima-sensei leave.<span class=\"pg\">p.176–182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> He showed up; he said nothing publicly; he witnessed the removal.<span class=\"pg\">p.175–182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Nagumo called him; Sakagami remembered.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryūen was just about to jump on Yagami-kun — Sakagami watched.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v8-p11-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami sakagami mentioned in passing named in this volume  passing mentions on pages  p 46  p 49  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v8-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">sakagami mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.11-208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in this volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mentions on pages: p.46, p.49.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y2v8-p46-1\">→ After: Boarding bus No.3 (Class C)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v8-p46-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami boarding bus no 3  class c  sakagami boards no 3  by class order a to d","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v8-p46-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Boarding bus No.3 (Class C)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.46<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakagami boards No.3 (by class order A to D).<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y2v8-p11-1\">← Before: sakagami mentioned in passing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y2v8-p49-1\">→ After: The bus assignments<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v8-p49-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami the bus assignments  mashima sensei was in charge of groups 1 through 5  chabashira sensei was in charge of groups 6 through 10  sakagami sensei was in charge of groups 11 through 15  and hoshinomiya sensei was in charge of groups 16 through 20","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v8-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The bus assignments<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.49<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Mashima-sensei was in charge of groups 1 through 5, Chabashira-sensei was in charge of groups 6 through 10, Sakagami-sensei was in charge of groups 11 through 15, and Hoshinomiya-sensei was in charge of groups 16 through 20.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y2v8-p46-1\">← Before: Boarding bus No.3 (Class C)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v9_5-p159-1","v":"y2v9.5","y":2,"o":26,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 6  sakagami sensei  sudo s growth crosses ayanokoji in the january 4 corridor  compliments sudo s academic growth  asks what moved class b  he attributes it to horikita  mentions class a looming  then to his staff meeting   he s shown an incredible growth rate since he enrolled   was it you who changed the class known as  defective  knows enough about the white room rumors to probe  deliberately deflects the lending history question  proud of sudo s growth  pokes his growth s origin and receives a non answer  his homeroom pride  the class s  defective  label may finally be broken","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v9_5-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: Sakagami-sensei: Sudō&#x27;s growth<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9.5 · p.159–161<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Crosses Ayanokōji in the January 4 corridor; compliments Sudō&#x27;s academic growth; asks what moved Class B; he attributes it to Horikita; mentions Class A looming; then to his staff meeting.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;He&#x27;s shown an incredible growth rate since he enrolled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Was it you who changed the class known as &#x27;defective&#x27;?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Knows enough about the White Room rumors to probe; deliberately deflects the lending-history question.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Proud of Sudō&#x27;s growth; pokes his growth&#x27;s origin and receives a non-answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.159–161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> His homeroom pride: the class&#x27;s &quot;defective&quot; label may finally be broken.<span class=\"pg\">p.159–161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v10-p9-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami sakagami mentioned in passing named in this volume  passing mention  locator pages  p 124  p 126 127  p 132  p 163  not line by line verified  substring false positives possible  not a scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v10-p9-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">sakagami mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.9-235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in this volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention (locator pages: p.124, p.126-127, p.132, p.163; not line-by-line verified; substring false positives possible). Not a scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y2v10-p124-1\">→ After: Ch.6: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v10-p124-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 6  passing mentions  locator cross check  passing mention   shortly after  sakagami sensei  ryuen s homeroom teacher  appeared in the passing mention   sakagami sensei signaled to start the special exam  passing mention   following horikita s instructions  sakagami sensei immediately reflected passing mention   sakagami sensei the names of her five protected members  passing mention   in a few minutes  sakagami sensei would signal the beginning of the 11th","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v10-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.124–163<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — Shortly after, Sakagami-sensei, Ryūen&#x27;s homeroom teacher, appeared in the<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — Sakagami-sensei signaled to start the special exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — Following Horikita&#x27;s instructions, Sakagami-sensei immediately reflected<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — Sakagami-sensei the names of her five protected members.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — In a few minutes, Sakagami-sensei would signal the beginning of the 11th<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakagami-y2v10-p9-1\">← Before: sakagami mentioned in passing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v11-p205-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru sakayanagi-arisu sakagami","q":"sakagami epilogue  the witness the career counseling room  he follows ryuen kakeru in  he does not know what is happening  he is asked to wait   a protection point is meaningless if we re voluntarily withdrawing  for fairness  it s been decided that we d request additional private points to fill the difference that the protection point makes  but the amount is kept to a minimum  if we take away his money  his class will really have nothing left  the protection point is meaningless  the withdrawal voids the contract  he knows what the contract means  he says nothing now  the homeroom teacher witnessing the contract  the end of year exam  the homeroom teacher witnessing the contract  the end of year exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v11-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: The witness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.205–209<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The career counseling room; he follows Ryūen Kakeru in; he does not know what is happening; he is asked to wait.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“A Protection Point is meaningless if we&#x27;re voluntarily withdrawing. For fairness, it&#x27;s been decided that we&#x27;d request additional private points to fill the difference that the Protection Point makes, but the amount is kept to a…”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A Protection Point is meaningless if we&#x27;re voluntarily withdrawing. For fairness, it&#x27;s been decided that we&#x27;d request additional private points to fill the difference that the Protection Point makes, but the amount is kept to a minimum. If we take away his money, his class will really have nothing left.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The Protection Point is meaningless; the withdrawal voids the contract; he knows what the contract means; he says nothing now.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The homeroom teacher witnessing the contract; the end-of-year exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.205–209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The homeroom teacher witnessing the contract; the end-of-year exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.205–209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v12-p65-1","v":"y2v12","y":2,"o":31,"k":"spoken","w":"sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 3  the body checks inside the special building s classroom  representatives seated on folding chairs  sakagami sensei and hoshinomiya sensei approach  sakagami holds an empty white case about 30 cm square  marked  2 b   please submit all phones  other metals  and electronic devices you have  she takes his phone  then horikita s and yosuke s  into the case  then performs the inspection herself from head to toes with a handheld metal detector  declares all three of them clear  says the phones will be returned after the exam   sorry  it s instructions from the school  okay  all three of you are clear   the phones we ve been entrusted with will be returned after the exam  please sit in the empty seats and wait  she is present when the discussion rules explanation begins  she holds the white cases  one per class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v12-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: The body checks<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12 · p.65–68<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Inside the special building&#x27;s classroom; representatives seated on folding chairs; Sakagami-sensei and Hoshinomiya-sensei approach; Sakagami holds an empty white case about 30 cm square, marked &quot;2-B.&quot; She takes his phone, then Horikita&#x27;s and Yōsuke&#x27;s, into the case; then performs the inspection herself from head to toes with a handheld metal detector; declares all three of them clear; says the phones will be returned after the exam.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Please submit all phones, other metals, and electronic devices you have.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sorry, it’s instructions from the school. Okay, all three of you are clear.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The phones we’ve been entrusted with will be returned after the exam. Please sit in the empty seats and wait.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is present when the discussion-rules explanation begins; she holds the white cases, one per class.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakagami-y2v12_5-p65-1","v":"y2v12.5","y":2,"o":32,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hoshinomiya-chie chabashira-sae sakagami","q":"sakagami ch 4  gathered at keyaki mall and mashima s room sakagami sensei in plain clothes approaches the meeting  as the one without a personal connection to the dispute  he is the impartial party   what s going on here  explain so we can understand   i see  but who is akiyama san  i don t recall such a student   in fact  i think hoshinomiya sensei didn t need to use the restroom  after talking to me  she went straight back to the waiting room   both of you are being quite lenient  even if it was an attempted issue  if it s true  it should be reported   don t jump to conclusions  i m not saying we need to report this to the school immediately   wanting to make your class win by any means necessary is unavoidable  given this school s system  this isn t something limited to just the students  even adults sometimes resort to dirty tactics  i myself have taken somewhat biased actions before  thinking it was for my class s sake   whether we report it or settle it among ourselves  we need to be cautious about the situation s credibility  we don t know if what ayanokoji kun is saying is true  it s only his testimony so far   i m not saying that  but we still need solid evidence  if it turns out hoshinomiya sensei was falsely accused of misconduct  she would be outraged  then  the people who doubted her  us  would be the ones in trouble  we can t predict what kind of punishment would be imposed   we can t say there s zero possibility that hoshinomiya sensei and ayanokoji kun have already conspired together  trying to set a trap for us  isn t that right  ayanokoji kun   given the way you re speaking  you have a good idea  don t you   no  that s the best approach  i think this is the most suitable method to verify whether she ll reveal the truth from her own mouth  chabashira sensei  that s fine with you  right   while i can t go so far as to tell you to rest assured  if we do catch hoshinomiya sensei attempting misconduct  and she decides to stop  i have no intention of escalating the matter   yes  if i play the villain in front of both of you here  it would leave me with concerns for next year  if my class ends up taking fire concentrated from all three classes and loses  it would be my responsibility   you re quite stubborn  aren t you  we wouldn t mind going ahead and reporting this to the higher ups  you know   i see  so that s your approach  indeed  if you behave from now on  hoshinomiya sensei  maybe there s no need to raise this as an issue   but if we don t interfere  we will report any violations we notice to the higher ups  you might be expelled from your position as a homeroom teacher  you know   i see  you seem to be truly resolved  but  i don t understand   then our discussion is over  let s disperse here  he verifies ayanokoji s testimony before acting  he declines to play the villain  he pressures her to comply or risk dismissal  he plays the impartial role opposite her old schoolmates","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakagami-y2v12_5-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: Gathered at Keyaki Mall and Mashima&#x27;s room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12.5 · p.65–76<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakagami-sensei in plain clothes approaches the meeting; as the one without a personal connection to the dispute, he is the impartial party.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What’s going on here? Explain so we can understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I see. But who is Akiyama-san? I don’t recall such a student.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In fact, I think Hoshinomiya-sensei didn’t need to use the restroom. After talking to me, she went straight back to the waiting room.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Both of you are being quite lenient, even if it was an attempted issue. If it’s true, it should be reported.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t jump to conclusions. I’m not saying we need to report this to the school immediately.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wanting to make your class win by any means necessary is unavoidable, given this school’s system. This isn’t something limited to just the students. Even adults sometimes resort to dirty tactics. I myself have taken somewhat biased actions before, thinking it was for my class’s sake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whether we report it or settle it among ourselves, we need to be cautious about the situation’s credibility. We don’t know if what Ayanokōji-kun is saying is true. It’s only his testimony so far.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not saying that, but we still need solid evidence. If it turns out Hoshinomiya-sensei was falsely accused of misconduct, she would be outraged. Then, the people who doubted her, us, would be the ones in trouble. We can’t predict what kind of punishment would be imposed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can’t say there’s zero possibility that Hoshinomiya-sensei and Ayanokōji-kun have already conspired together, trying to set a trap for us. Isn’t that right, Ayanokōji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Given the way you’re speaking, you have a good idea, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, that’s the best approach. I think this is the most suitable method to verify whether she’ll reveal the truth from her own mouth. Chabashira-sensei, that’s fine with you, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “While I can’t go so far as to tell you to rest assured, if we do catch Hoshinomiya-sensei attempting misconduct, and she decides to stop, I have no intention of escalating the matter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. If I play the villain in front of both of you here, it would leave me with concerns for next year. If my class ends up taking fire concentrated from all three classes and loses, it would be my responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re quite stubborn, aren’t you? We wouldn’t mind going ahead and reporting this to the higher-ups, you know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see, so that’s your approach. Indeed, if you behave from now on, Hoshinomiya-sensei, maybe there’s no need to raise this as an issue.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if we don’t interfere, we will report any violations we notice to the higher-ups. You might be expelled from your position as a homeroom teacher, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. You seem to be truly resolved, but... I don’t understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then our discussion is over. Let’s disperse here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He verifies Ayanokōji&#x27;s testimony before acting; he declines to play the villain.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> He pressures her to comply or risk dismissal.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> He plays the impartial role opposite her old schoolmates.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"}];
